{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - User - MFA - Potential Okta MFA Bombing via Push Notifications [table]",
	"Description": "Finds accounts sent a burst of MFA push notifications, especially where the user denied some. MFA fatigue attacks work by holding a valid password and hammering the push prompt until the victim taps approve to make it stop, so a high push count with denials in it is the attack in progress.\n\nThresholds: 5 or more push sends, or 2 or more explicit denials, per account. Edit the eval near the end of the query to tune them.\n\nThis detection uses stats, so it renders as a table rather than shipping raw entries.\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/credential_access_potential_okta_mfa_bombing_via_push_notifications/\n- https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/tree/main/rules/integrations/okta/credential_access_potential_okta_mfa_bombing_via_push_notifications.toml\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
	"ScheduledType": "search",
	"GUID": "7d0df654-f8cb-57cb-a326-4f357d67d1c9",
	"SearchReference": "8a188024-aec5-5258-b6d2-68ab8941c403"
